# Testing

## Tools
- pytest — Python unit + integration tests
- Vitest — frontend unit tests
- Playwright — E2E tests (post-MVP)

## Database isolation
| Test type | Postgres port | Workers |
|---|---|---|
| Library unit | none (MemoryStore) | — |
| Server unit | none (mock library) | — |
| Server integration | 5436 | 1 |
| E2E | 5437 | 1 |
| Library unit (parallel) | 5435 + 5438–5440 | 4 |

## Library tests (`packages/dqt/tests/`)
- Must run without Postgres, Redis, or network.
- Use `MemoryStore` and offline fixture data.
- Must complete in <60s.

**Per-detector requirements** (5 tests each):
1. Known-answer test against a textbook example.
2. Behaviour tests on synthetic distributions (drift / no-drift, anomaly / no-anomaly).
3. `hypothesis` property test for numerical stability (no NaN/Inf, bounded scores).
4. Golden-file test for `STAT_SCALE` verdict (pass/warn/fail boundary).
5. Time-series detectors: seasonality and trend robustness test.

## Adapter tests (`packages/dqt/tests/adapters/`)
- Real engines via testcontainers (Postgres, MySQL, ClickHouse).
- Recorded fixtures via vcrpy (BigQuery, Snowflake — no credentials in CI).
- Marker: `@pytest.mark.adapter`.

## Server tests (`apps/server/tests/`)
- **Unit**: mock the library. Test route logic, auth, error handling, tenant scoping.
- **Integration**: real library + testcontainers Postgres (port 5436). Test actual DB behaviour.
- Marker: `@pytest.mark.unit` / `@pytest.mark.integration`.

## Auth in server tests
Dependency-override `get_current_user` with a fixture user. **Never patch middleware.**
```python
app.dependency_overrides[get_current_user] = lambda: fixture_admin_user
```

## Frontend tests (`apps/web/`)
Vitest for component unit tests. Test rendering, user interactions, error states. No Playwright in MVP.

## Pytest markers
```python
@pytest.mark.unit        # no external deps
@pytest.mark.integration # needs real DB
@pytest.mark.adapter     # needs real warehouse or vcrpy fixture
@pytest.mark.slow        # takes >5s
```

## Test data
```
tests/data/
├── warehouses/          # SQLite/DuckDB fixtures simulating warehouse schemas
├── dbt_artifacts/       # sample manifest.json, catalog.json
└── golden_outputs/      # expected DetectorResult JSON for golden-file tests
```

## Commands
```bash
make test-lib              # library unit tests (<60s)
make test-server-unit      # server unit tests
make test-server-int       # server integration tests (starts testcontainer)
make test-adapter          # adapter tests
make test-web              # frontend Vitest tests
make test-all              # everything

# Fast iteration flags
./tests/run_unit_tests.sh --skip-db-reset --skip-schema-gen
```

## Best practices
- Test the real library in integration tests — don't mock detectors.
- Pytest style (functions + fixtures), not unittest class style.
- Use `pytest.approx` for float comparisons.
- Test names: `test_<method>_<scenario>` (e.g. `test_wasserstein1_detects_distribution_shift`).
